[[Face it - Intro]]


:: Light up the candle {"position":"300,400","size":"100,100"}

<img src="https://64.media.tumblr.com/59e43d6535bc43036be8b7a264a03be3/527e9990a7192707-5c/s2048x3072/a3b99e7469b6eadde4fa2e9ce3c50cb95bfeab70.pnj" width="666" height="auto">


<p><em>– Show your face, demon!</em> – she proclaims with a sense of fury as the sulfuric smoke of a struck match briefly poisons the air.
<img src="https://64.media.tumblr.com/597faf750c7117fe55214c414d9ed20a/527e9990a7192707-60/s2048x3072/e4ef5080aedaa49d0c4aaa4aa3b8831e368bf0a9.pnj" width="666" height="auto">
Her dark, tired eyes peer upon the aquarium glass, pierce through the distorted features of a creature hidden within. 
<img src="https://64.media.tumblr.com/8065e7b302d366b566d627b9b1cf29b7/527e9990a7192707-cd/s2048x3072/4f92d986800aed0736c5b83339a51710dd177eed.pnj" width="666" height="auto">
What appeared to be a mere guppy moments ago grew a body with a befittingly devilish smug, toothy grin and prying predatory gaze. 

<img src="https://64.media.tumblr.com/887796ad6c0038206aaa3195b46943b4/527e9990a7192707-98/s2048x3072/f68d970831f44c493782b99266a831a6e0d45d98.pnj" width="666" height="auto">
Red as blood, frightful as nightmares it plagues the poor souls with, its presence alone rendered hairs on Willow's back standing.<br />
<img src="https://64.media.tumblr.com/f05b998712ebb7378b8871d6dbf820ab/527e9990a7192707-60/s2048x3072/05a512baf0753d98c7564e4c906fb7ae6789febf.pnj" width="666" height="auto">
But she can't back away just because the demon truly proved to be real.</p>

<p><strong><em>– Willow Blue... So you see me now, child... How delicious.</em> </strong></p>

<p>Its cold voice alone could sent her shivering; every word Grinmaw chose was carefully weighed, measured and delivered with exact degree of soul-crushing condescendence it chose to make obvious to her. Its body emerged behind the glass in a triumphal display of it's features — as if it was an embodiment of an ancient deity paraded by the human race long time ago.</p>

<p>Willow's brows furrowed as she steeled her resolve. The Juju Guppy refused to see itself a mere captive trophy in Lucas's aquarium; rather, it triumphed that it managed to get itself oh-so-close to a sinful man. Yet it chose to torment the innocent and latched onto his past lover — so-called voodoo queen prayed, at least, it was Grinmaw's decision alone.</p>

<p>–<em> It's you who has been calling to Tequila in the night,</em> – she accused demon sharply, standing before his enclosure with a practiced determination of a tiger tamer cracking their whip.</p>

<p>– <strong><em>Ha-ha! I whisper so sweetly to her.</em></strong> – it splits its grin open like the gates of Hell, carrying its husky laugh into a conspirator's whisper, – <strong><em>It's just a matter of time.</em></strong></p>

<p>Willow strikes herself in the chest, fists closed so tight that her knuckles turn bloodless pale. She peered into the great darkness many times before on her own and came out victorious — she is ready to do it again, for the sake of the other. – <em>Swamp blood runs in these veins –</em> she fulminates, eyes burning in determination, – <em>and I will end your reign here. </em></p>

<p>The demon hisses a snicker through its teeth before it lets itself roar in a deafening sardonic laugh. It wheezes and batters behind the aquarium glass, so full of itself, so pleased with the offered display.</p>

<p>–<strong><em> Ha HAAA! I should have known! You ARE powerful! – </em></strong>its face settles with a challenging smirk as it eyes Willow like a particularly appealing dessert, – <em><strong>But a drop of voodoo blood, against the darkness of this place? Frankly put, I don't think you're </strong></em><strong>quite</strong><em><strong> above the cut for it.</strong></em></p>

<p>–<em> The darkness? But...</em> – she is taken aback in a moment of confusion, but quickly finds her grip, – <em>It's you. YOU are the poison that I will—</em></p>

<p>–<strong><em> You will NOTHING! </em></strong>– it snaps, its teeth tearing open at her wavering image reflected twice in the thickness of aquarium glass; it peers upon her with a fury of a spirit whose power was boasted to be contained outright inside a thoughtless fetish, – <strong><em>You don't even see what you're up against, girl! As you are, you can't even begin to reach my world! But I DO like your overconfidence! I can give you a taste of what you claim to be up for!</em></strong></p>

<p>Before Willow mustered to object to the demon's cruel words, her senses were snuffed out like a wick of a candlelight.<br />
Being a voodoo practitioner, it was far from her first rodeo to be mounted with a spirit; but the way Grinmaw took over her vessel could only compare to a bronc busting. She was thrown out of her body without so much as a chance to rebuke, not as much possessed as straight-up turned zombie by an evil-spirited bokor. As her mind went adrift as if leased by the poison of datura, the cruel hands of Juju Guppy's spirit made sure to drag her fractured and cast away soul through everything that hurt. She looked, but not through her eyes; she saw a body just like hers, but it didn't belong to Willow. All the now-dead she shared her path with fleeting moments of living ago, those with whom she shared and shed her blood as she found her calling in the dear priesthood of her people. Imagery, so familiar, twisted against her, pried open with a curse like a gushing, unhealing wound. Half her soul, torn away and departed from her early, now calling for it's due reunion.<br />
Was her soul bound to body of hers still, or was it standing at the crossroad before the Papa Legba? Was she the twin doll in her arms, or was she one hung off the Kapok tree? Was her body standing before Grinmaw still, or was it hanging loose, ringing a bell for the spirit, untethering?</p>

<p>...Was there anything left for her in her husk of a body to hold on to begin with?</p>

<p>—<strong><em> You are mine, Willow Blue. All of them here are mine. </em></strong>– it sings with cruel resignation, as if a mother telling her child it will not see the light of day again, as it narrows it's eyes into a sharp, disgruntled slit, – <strong><em>And I am HIS.</em></strong></p>

<p>Grinmaw falls silent for a moment, tasting the hundred times uttered words in its mouth as if they suddenly make it want to wince. Cycle after cycle. Year after year. It played along with Lucas's dumb game of self-torment, still stuck inside the glass fish tank playing its petty side-role. Brought the death upon the same two guests over and over, compelling both to step closer to the ledger of their doom. Was this petty dollhouse masquerade really all it was good for? In a split of a second, its mind, euphoric in its claim, let out like a dwarf in a flask and left free to roam as it desires, dreamt of a greedy thought, something far more alluring.<br />
Does it <em> have to</em> be HIS? Or could Bondes <em>truly</em> be ITS?</p>

<p>–<em> N.. No! – </em>The voodoo queen barely manages to utter the words in her protest, holding onto the last bits of what her body gives her, – <em>You are poison! You are... You...</em></p>

<p><em>– <strong>Sweet Willow... You have me all wrong, </strong></em>– Juju Guppy offers a polite, patient smile, it's presence echoing inside of Willow's body as much as it was beaming from behind the glass, – <em><strong>I'm NOT the stab in the guts, child. NOR am I the TEETH at the throat. I may be the demon, but I am FAR more modest than the evil that needlessly tortures your souls in this wretched place. </strong></em></p>

<p>–<em> I... I hear you. – </em>she whispers back, broken, body not quite her own.</p>

<p><em>– <strong>I am tired of this poor treatment, see, and I want to offer you a way out of this, my love. Bring the stop to your endless fall. </strong></em></p>

<p>It assaulted her with a vision unlike anything she knew; painted pictures of fire engulfing the mansion whole, of the cruel death brought upon its attendees all too soon. It shook her with the visages of a red king, a golden skull, a skinless woman and a man in a crooked bird mask holding them like voodoo dolls, chanting upon their spirits for the purpose of his very own torment. It brought terror upon her — sudden knowledge that everyone within these walls is a subject of their own elaborate and cruel death trap.</p>

<p>It was also far too much for her mind to bear all at once.</p>

<p>–<em> ...but a true voodoo queen must die before she can open her eyes to the ways of the ghosts,</em> – Grinmaw laughed, observing the ruined state of it's broken down vessel, – <strong><em>So you will play your part at my hands, from now and forever on.</em></strong></p>

<p>She walked out of the room, blinded by pale blue fire that left her bare soul exposed. She stepped along the dead as she made her way through her familiar streets, down to the coffin, up to the Kapok tree where her twin's duppie still stays restless. The candles shone light upon the faces of dead and dear ones for her alright. Yet there were so many words left unsaid between them, so many things left undone... She missed her. She missed her so much. So why would she resist coming back to her loving embrace? Why would anyone?</p>

<img src="https://64.media.tumblr.com/d61ea55a8a1d0af3f95099006fd6191b/527e9990a7192707-34/s1280x1920/a6b35210b52f23e941581708233451b9f2b8ea5f.jpg" width="666" height="auto">

<p>With a rope pulling tight in her arms, just like twine holding twin doll so close to her, she embraced the path that was laid out for her so clear.</p>

<p align="center"><strong><em>[[And when I'll bring you back, everyone will be waiting for you, my sweet Willow.|Chapter 2: Scope of the Issue]]</em></strong></p>


